# Front-End Dev-Mode: Subsystem Implementation

## Purpose

This file provides specialized guidance for implementing specific subsystems within front-end applications. It focuses on isolating subsystem implementation from the broader application while ensuring proper integration with the overall system.

## Usage as Project-Rule-Parameter

This file contains subsystem implementation patterns for front-end development and should be referenced in message-commands when implementing specific front-end subsystems:

```
dev-mode: front-end-workflow @parameters/front-end/dev-mode/dev-mode-subsystem.mdc
```

## Implementation Strategy

The subsystem implementation strategy follows a focused approach:

### 1. Subsystem Analysis Phase

Begin by analyzing the subsystem to understand its scope, boundaries, and integration points:

```typescript
// 1. Access architecture patterns
fetch_rules(["knowledge/patterns/impl/architecture-patterns"], 
           "Understanding architectural patterns for subsystem implementation")

// 2. Identify subsystem boundaries
codebase_search("related components to subsystem", ["front-end/src/components"])

// 3. Examine state management approach
grep_search("useContext|createContext|Provider.*Subsystem", false, "*.tsx")

// 4. Analyze subsystem API integration
grep_search("api\\..*Subsystem|fetch.*Subsystem", false, "*.tsx")

// 5. Check existing subsystem implementation patterns
codebase_search("subsystem implementation pattern", ["front-end/src"])
```

